<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">638 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hong was fought in 638 BCE on the Hong River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> between the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> and the State of Chu. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-xiang-of-song">Duke Xiang of Song</a> refused to attack the Chu army while it was crossing the river or before it had formed up, and was heavily defeated and wounded. The episode became a byword for misplaced chivalry and ended Song's bid for hegemony.</p></div>
